{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review","id":1539465,"title":"W5 videogame/visual novel \"WtA: Purgatory\" - Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-29T05:51:00-07:00","id":1539465,"title":"W5 videogame/visual novel \"WtA: Purgatory\" - Review","content":"A lot has changed since Heart of the Forest, the prequel to this game, came out a few years ago. At the time of that release, the W5 corebook was still being developed by Hunters Entertainment. Since then, a quite different W5 corebook saw the light of day and in that environment, we\u2019ve now gotten a sequel to Heart of the Forest named Purgatory.<br /> <br /> On the surface some things stayed the same: We follow one Garou-protagonist, we get a visual novel based on narrative choices and managing various stats, the art-style is still the same and the Polish setting is still the Bia\u0142owie\u017ca Forest (at least in part in this game). What this game introduces is a new protagonist in the form of Samira (an Afghani refugee) and the Warsaw Sept.<br /> <br /> The story in this game can be neatly broken down into two routes. Early on, you\u2019re presented with two problems the Warsaw Sept faces and you have to decide which one you follow up on. I think one thing that surprised me during my first playthrough was how short this game is. Because the game essentially bifurcates during that choice. You can only do one route and when you\u2019re finished with that problem, the game ends. My first playthrough lasted about two and a half hours but because of the overlap that happens in both routes, I got through my second playthrough in roughly ninety minutes. So this isn\u2019t a long game by any stretch of the imagination.<br /> <br /> The game also doesn\u2019t exactly follow the script from the released W5 corebook. But at this point, I feel like a broken record mentioning that. On one hand, I\u2019m glad none of the W5 media is interested in trying to replicate the presentation from the released W5 corebook. On the other hand, I think it\u2019s safe to say that there\u2019s no consistency when it comes to W5. Personally, I like the setting presented in this game more than the one presented in the W5 corebook, though.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">The Game</span><br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1429\" height=\"795\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/F3B0SDG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/F3B0SDG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/F3B0SDG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> This screenshot is from my second playthrough. It\u2019s less about the actual text but more about a moment in the game where you can see most of the things that go on in this game.<br /> <br /> On the right side you see some art that depicts what is going on. The art-style is okay, I think. The Bane-Spirits look interesting but there was never anything in the game that wowed me. It works and doesn\u2019t distract in a negative sense.<br /> <br /> Now as to the actual game-mechanics. It\u2019s a bit different from Heart of the Forest. During character-creation you\u2019re first asked to pick one physical Skill and one mental Skill. These are more like specializations, though. And really, what you\u2019re actually picking is options for flavor-text. The actual events in the game are pretty much on rails (more on that later). So the difference between picking either Stealth or Athletics is that you get the option for flavor-text depending on whether you picked the former or the latter.<br /> <br /> The same applies to Tribe. For my first playthrough my Samira was a Silver Fang Philodox and the second time around I chose her to be a Black Fury Theurge. You get this flavor-text that is sign-posted by the Tribe-name like in the screenshot. The plot doesn\u2019t really change. Events aren\u2019t impacted by the Tribe-choice. That is disappointing. Then again, it has to be said that as a purely flavor-oriented thing it works quite well. The reason for that is that these flavor-influenced texts show up quite often. It actually happened so often that Silver Fang Samira was a different person compared to Black Fury Samira. In the case of the former, the text mentioned how Samira dreamed of one day attaining a leadership-position in the Sept and when she interacted with her companion, she was authoritative and decisive, treating her companion more like an underling. Meanwhile, as a Black Fury it talked about how she desired to make a change in the world and she was always impatient with her companion, urging to just make a decision and get back to the action. For example, in the screenshot you see the Black Fury version whereas in the Silver Fang version Samira actively went to the Sept asking for a fake-ID and then with their support went to the Glass Walkers and told them to make one for her. So that works quite well.<br /> <br /> The same applies to the chosen Auspice and Renown. Although with the latter, it has to be said that \u201cRenown\u201d is the wrong word for it (the W5 corebook\u2019s approach to Renown has the same issue). Rather it\u2019s about Glory, Honor and Wisdom presenting various ideals and virtues on how to deal with various situations. And so, you get moments where you can choose how to approach a situation, then depending on what you pick, you either get a dot in Glory, Honor or Wisdom. And then occasionally you get flavor-text based on whatever your highest Renown is that shows how your character analyzes a scene and what has happened. Again, it\u2019s just there to be flavor.<br /> <br /> This worked well for my playthroughs but I can see that you can potentially stumble into combinations of Tribe, Auspice and Renown where descriptions contradict each other. In a way, this presentation banks on building your Samira in rather stereotypical ways. A Glass Walker Ragabash works better in what the game gives you than a Silver Fang Ragabash, for example.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s get to the trackers at the top. Both Willpower and Health are tracks that just go up and down depending on choices. Losing Health without going to zero means you take a hit in combat or another situation without being badly affected. Willpower is something you occasionally have to spend to pick certain (good) options in a situation.<br /> <br /> Then you got Rage and Harano. There are still options which increase or decrease those trackers but more importantly is that you get flavor-texts based on where your tracker is at the moment. The categories are: Zero (self-explanatory), Low (1 \u2013 2), Balanced ( 3 ), High (4 \u2013 5).<br /> <br /> With Harano it\u2019s pretty obvious: the less the better. How this shows in the flavor-text is that the higher the Harano, the more Samira\u2019s thoughts turn more introverted and anxiety-driven whereas she opens up at the lower end and becomes more empathetic. It\u2019s well written\u2026 although it does do the thing of Harano=depression which I\u2019m not a huge fan of. But as a way to describe depression, it\u2019s done well (more on that later when I talk about Samira as a character). Also, I think this system would be something the TTRPG would\u2019ve benefited from. Especially because this kind of categorization already existed anyway with Humanity in V5. Another thing Renegade should probably introduce in a future supplement.<br /> <br /> Rage also works well in that regard as the flavor-text makes quite clear how high-strung and aggressive Samira is at the High-rating. Meanwhile, in the lower ratings Samira feels drained and unenthusiastic. It\u2019s interesting that this game positions Rage 3 (Balanced) as the good place to be. So Rage isn\u2019t positioned as inherently bad.<br /> <br /> The other two things left to talk about is character-relationships and Gifts/Items. Relationships exist on a -3 to +3 scale. Does it matter? Again, it\u2019s mostly flavor-text so the differences you can make with your choices are miniscule. Gifts/Items are one-use-only things \u2013 which is completely fine. Conceptually I would take issue with this but this game is so short that it didn\u2019t bother me. For example, in my first playthrough with Silver Fang Philodox Garou I never used a Gift. Whenever the game presents the opportunity to use a Gift/item, you should just do it because there won\u2019t be some other time to use it elsewhere in the story anyway.<br /> <br /> I also have to say that managing all the trackers in this game was easy. That screenshot you see is near the end and as you can see that\u2019s exactly the stats you would want heading into the last third of the game. So, the game\u2019s pretty forgiving and easy when it comes to avoiding failure-states.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">The Story</span><br /> <br /> But what\u2019s Purgatory even about, you may wonder\u2026 Let\u2019s start with the setting.<br /> <br /> (I don\u2019t go over all the details of the story and events in the game but if you absolutely do not want any <b>spoilers</b>, you should probably stop reading here)<br /> <br /> In this game\u2019s setting you deal with three Septs. You got the Warsaw Sept, the Bia\u0142owie\u017ca Forest Sept and the Sept in Afghanistan that Samira used to belong to. Each Sept has a caern and each caern is protected by multiple (!) Garou-packs. In fact, part of character-creation is to choose between three Packs which each have their own dedicated Pack-Patron-Spirit. There\u2019s no talk of \u201cThe Garou Nation has fallen\u201d anywhere in the game. One thing I also really like is that two character-relationship-trackers you have in the game are the Warsaw-caern and the Bia\u0142owie\u017ca forest. And the game shows off that these are spiritual entities which can help you! These are conscious entities you can interact with. It\u2019s a bit sad how the W5 corebook downplayed that.<br /> <br /> Also, it should be kept in mind that whatever elements I talk about below have to be seen in the context of a rather short game. In general, a big problem for the narrative is that it takes on quite a lot of things at the same time and due to its short length none get the proper attention.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Samira</span><br /> <br /> Aside from the flavor-options I mentioned there\u2019s of course one that\u2019s the most important to the game\u2019s story: Samira is an Afghan refugee in Poland. There are flashbacks/dream-sequences that describe the journey of fleeing Afghanistan and getting to Poland.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, the game starts with the final border-crossing in which Samira\u2019s little brother gets killed. And this leads to one of the more interesting elements in the story: When the first Chapter starts, Samira has already been in Poland for about a year but hasn\u2019t been active in the Sept. And that is because at the start of this game, Samira is in Harano. So, on one level Samira\u2019s story-arc in this visual novel is about her getting out of Harano and becoming an active member of the Sept again. Of course, if the game had listened to the W5 corebook, she should\u2019ve been declared an unplayable irreversibly doomed character the second she fell to Harano (lol)\u2026<br /> <br /> The Afghanistan-element especially suffers due to the short length. While the flashbacks talk about weeks of travel, it really does give the appearance of a short journey. Like, you\u2019re in Afghanistan, you travel to a nearby city, go through the mountains, cross a river and\u2026 voila, you\u2019re at the Polish border. Later on, her uncle also arrives and it just enhances this feeling when he writes a letter saying \u201cHey, I had to leave. I\u2019m coming to you.\u201d And then a few days later, he really is already at the Polish border.<br /> <br /> The descriptions of Afghanistan also don\u2019t work that well because the focus is entirely on the US leaving Afghanistan in 2021 and the Taliban taking over. For one, being a civilian in Afghanistan in the years prior hadn\u2019t been exactly a cakewalk either. And the text makes it seem like the Taliban are these space-invaders that left before and only now in 2021 reappeared.<br /> <br /> What the game also does is completely sidestep the religious angle. Instead, in another way where it ignores the W5 corebook and goes with the old lore, this game\u2019s setting still firmly believes in Garou being mainly a hereditary thing and so Samira is growing up in a family of Garou. Kinfolk is never mentioned but it\u2019s essentially what is described. Her aunt is a Garou and is the first person to move to Warsaw. But part of this is that the game states that because they\u2019re a Garou-family, they didn\u2019t grow up as Muslims and don\u2019t practice those beliefs/traditions (like covering your hair) and instead they grew up believing in the Litany. That\u2019s how it\u2019s phrased. There\u2019s a flashback-scene tied to this where Samira forgot to cover her hair after leaving the home and is confronted by Taliban-soldiers. The game is more interested in sidestepping that conversation than having any sort of take on it, though.<br /> <br /> Overall, this leads to Samira as an Afghan refugee being more about her character being an outsider in Poland who came there as a refugee in a general sense. It\u2019s more about Poland\u2019s reaction to it rather than delving into the experiences and regional history of the country Samira came from. Due to how little this gets explored, you could\u2019ve easily made her a Syrian or Libyan. There\u2019s no discussion of the war in Afghanistan that started in 2001, for example. Thinking about it, I think this would\u2019ve worked better if she had been the younger sibling who as a kid came with the older sibling to the border, then the older sibling gets killed, the younger sibling experiences their First Change. That way you could narratively justify why the Afghanistan/Islam-angle is being downplayed and not explored in detail.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Missions</span><br /> <br /> It starts with Samira going to the Sept and meeting Illona who\u2019s the Sept-leader. On the way there, you encounter a weak Bane-Spirit that flees from you. At the Sept you find out that a Glass Walker Garou had been found murdered. Then, Andrej a Shadow Lord Garou arrives and angrily berates Illona for not taking action. Andrej is a blonde, blue-eyed guy who\u2019s angry and abrasive while also claiming that the increased presence of Wyrm-minions and Bane-Spirits in the city is all due to the increased number of refugees. If you know W5, you can already see where this is going\u2026<br /> <br /> In fact, I was a bit surprised when something was changed here compared to the Demo that came out a few months ago. In the Demo, part of Andrej\u2019s abrasiveness was that he started his rant by dead-naming the Sept-leader (Illona is a trans-woman). That was already a bit of a weird choice (they introduced a trans-character just to immediately dead-name her\u2026?). But the part that bugged me the most is that Samira\u2019s POV had been all about her having zero idea what was going on. I mean, come on! The line from Andrej was \u201cMikhal\u2026 or should I say Illona?\u201d. Also, this should\u2019ve led to an immediate confrontation because it went way beyond mere provocative. So, it\u2019s good that they removed that bit from the released version.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Samira goes to the Apokolipsa-Bar (the name is a bit on the nose\u2026) where she works part-time. There she meets Pat, Victoria and Aleksander. And you essentially get the two missions in this game. You can only pick one. Pat\u2019s route is about investigating the death of the Glass Walker and Aleksander\u2019s route is about investigating Andrej.<br /> <br /> Remember how I mentioned in the other thread how W5 only knows how to tell two stories? This game falls perfectly in these two categories. Pat\u2019s route is about bad people doing bad stuff (and they happen to be Fomori) and Aleksander\u2019s route is about Garou doing the wrong thing (because they\u2019re too angry and/or sad).<br /> <br /> I mentioned at the beginning how much of the character-creation-options are just about flavor-text and this shows in these two routes because they\u2019re essentially on rails. There\u2019s little that happens where you can deviate from the general plot-structure. Additionally, both routes have the same structure.<br /> <br /> It goes like this:<br /> <br /> Investigation-scenes --&gt;Infiltration/Investigation Site A--&gt;Fight with minion after leaving Site A--&gt;Train-ride to Bia\u0142owie\u017ca Forest (Samira finds out that Tariq, her uncle, is coming to the Polish border)--&gt;Fight with two minions in the train\uf0e0Small town scene with protestors against refugees/talk with Journalist/NGO worker--&gt;Talk with Winter Weasel Spirit--&gt;Infiltration/Investigation Site B--&gt;Talk with the Wolf Mother Spirit--&gt;Final confrontation (You either can fight the big bad, his minions or protect the refugees trying to cross the border\u2026 and you still save the refugees even if you don\u2019t pick that last option)<br /> <br /> In both routes, these are interspersed with flashbacks/dream-sequences that are tying back to the Wolf-mother/Wolf-father conflict in the story.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Pat\u2019s route</span><br /> <br /> Pat is a hacktivist Glass Walker Garou who\u2019s investigating the death of Emyr, a fellow Glass Walker. You do the investigation of the murder-scene which leads to a nearby refugee-center. You learn from the people in the refugees that Emyr was investigating a nearby factory. Then the refugee-center gets suddenly attacked by teen-vandals (they throw rocks to break the windows). After you\u2019ve chased off the teenage-vandals, you follow them and find out that the owner of the nearby factory is paying them to vandalize refugee-centers in Warsaw. Also, the owner is a Fomor.<br /> <br /> You infiltrate the factory and learn about how the factory is producing weapons and cameras for a private military company and you learn that an attack on refugees trying to cross is planned. When you leave, you\u2019re confronted by a Fomor. Then you travel to the forest-Sept. On the train you get attacked by two Fomori. Once you get to the small town, you meet up with Maia (the protagonist from the first game) who is the current Sept leader of the forest-Sept and the trail leads to the mentioned private military-base. You infiltrate that, learn of where the attack will take place and then you basically get to the final confrontration where soldiers led by Fomori are trying to deliberately kill refugees trying to cross the border.<br /> <br /> This was the first playthrough I did and I can\u2019t stress enough just how abrupt the ending felt. You kill the bad guys, protect the refugees and then the story just kinda ends\u2026 This one also felt like the less impactful of the two stories. It\u2019s just all about bad people doing bad stuff. There\u2019s a bad company with a factory, there are bad politicians getting bribes from the company who are anti-refugees and then you got the military-base full of soldiers willing to just hunt down and kill a bunch of refugees. And the soldiers are led by Fomori, of course.<br /> <br /> You have that talk with the Wolfmother-spirit which talks about the Wyrm being ascendant but there\u2019s no talk of an \u201cAge of Apocalypse\u201d. One thing I liked about this part is that writing makes clear here that the human evil doesn\u2019t just get exploited by the Wyrm but it pushes the evil in the world to expand as well. This isn\u2019t the take you get in W5 where it\u2019s all humanity\u2019s fault and the Wyrm would be powerless to further any of its evil agenda if humanity were just a little bit nicer. There\u2019s a push and pull between humanity and the Wyrm that goes in both directions. The setting just feels more spiritual when the Wyrm is depicted like that, I think.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Aleksander\u2019s route</span><br /> <br /> You can kinda see what this one\u2019s about but it doesn\u2019t play out exactly the way you\u2019d think. So Andrej, the main-villain of this route is a Shadow Lord and the leader of the Wolf-father-Pack. I took a screenshot of how it\u2019s described in the game:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1428\" height=\"795\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/RuLpDbk.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/RuLpDbk.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/RuLpDbk.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> Andrej\u2019s whole take on the situation is that there is only one reason why the Wyrm has gotten stronger in Warsaw and it\u2019s the refugees. So the investigation starts with checking out the location where supposedly a member of Andrej\u2019s pack has been attacked by a refugee who was also a Fomor. You find Zuzanna at the location and it quickly becomes clear that she lied about the attack because Andrej told her to do so (you later find out that she\u2019s being abused by Andrej as well).<br /> <br /> At this point, I wondered whether this is a setting without the Cult of Fenris. The first place you infiltrate is the den of the Wolf-father\u2019s Pack and Andrej is giving an anti-refugee speech to a bunch of Garou. The whole thing also had the whiff of a cult. But to my surprise when you search Andrej\u2019s room you find a book \u2013 which is all about the ideals and goals of the Cult of Fenris. That\u2019s right, you don\u2019t get the Cult of Fenris but instead you get this Wolf-father-Pack which uses this book like a manual to imitate the Cult. It feels odd. So it\u2019s exactly like the Cult of Fenris \u2013 except it isn\u2019t the Cult of Fenris\u2026?<br /> <br /> It gets even weirder with the Wolfmother-scene on this route. Because it\u2019s here and only here where Hauglosk gets mentioned. Nobody but the Wolfmother-spirit in this setting seems to be aware that Hauglosk is even a thing. Also, she explains that the Wolf-Spirit has fallen and split in two. What used to be two halves functioning in unity has been disrupted. The Wolf-father-Spirit who used to be about lashing out at the enemies of the pack and keeping the hearth safe has been consumed by Rage and has now turned into a vindictive and cruel Spirit. That actually felt like a better origin-story for something like a Cult of Fenris. And you wouldn\u2019t have a whole Tribe fall as one but instead split into two factions. Meanwhile, the Cult of Fenris isn\u2019t just members of that one fallen Tribe but as the name implies an actual cult that any Garou who has the same ideals and beliefs can join.<br /> <br /> But the ending of this route is also a letdown. Andrej and his Garou-followers are attacking and trying to kill a bunch of refugees that try to cross the border. I thought there would be more to this because Aleksander as it turned out used to be Andrej\u2019s boyfriend. So I picked the route where you directly fight with Andrej. But the fight\u2019s pretty anticlimactic. He\u2019s bad, you\u2019re good, Samira and Aleksander beat the crap out of him (the worst that can happen here is that you don\u2019t beat him outright but get him to flee). If you\u2019re successful, you knock him unconscious, drag him back to the Warsaw Sept where he gets executed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Conclusion</span><br /> <br /> I had a great time during my first playthrough \u2013 until I had gotten to the ending. I was completely unprepared for that. First, I thought that after killing the soldiers and Fomori who targeted the refugees, it would go on to be about Samira &amp; co thoroughly taking apart the Fomori led private military and factory. So the ending felt quite abrupt. Second, I imagined that after I would be done with that part, the game would move on to let me play through Aleksander\u2019s story. Neither happened. Instead, you got more of a bland \u201cAll\u2019s well that ends well\u2026\u201d kind of summary. And there\u2019s even this line about how the story you didn\u2019t pick at the beginning would just remain a mystery. So, if you\u2019re doing Pat\u2019s route, it said that Andrej\u2019s dark secret remained hidden while if you\u2019re doing Aleksander\u2019s route it said that Emyr\u2019s death remained a mystery. Very unfulfilling\u2026<br /> <br /> The next shock came when during my second playthrough I realized just how on rails the story actually was and how little impact your choices had on the adventure. Your choices were more about what sort of flavor-text the game would give you rather than actually changing the course of the narrative.<br /> <br /> But if you can get past these two issues, the one strength it has is that it nails the tone of a WtA-game quite well. Spirits are important, there are plenty of Garou characters and it\u2019s emphasized that they\u2019re a tight-knit community. Tonally this game is much closer to what I would want out of a WtA-story than what we\u2019d seen with other W5 material.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T13:17:33-07:00","id":1539495,"title":"","content":"I've seen it on the Switch weekly news and was looking for some review to decide what to do. So thanks!<br /> <br /> Being short is the worse downside for me. I'll either wait for a discount or pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T17:49:39-07:00","id":1539511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review#post1539465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It gets even weirder with the Wolfmother-scene on this route. Because it\u2019s here and only here where Hauglosk gets mentioned. Nobody but the Wolfmother-spirit in this setting seems to be aware that Hauglosk is even a thing. Also, she explains that the Wolf-Spirit has fallen and split in two. What used to be two halves functioning in unity has been disrupted. The Wolf-father-Spirit who used to be about lashing out at the enemies of the pack and keeping the hearth safe has been consumed by Rage and has now turned into a vindictive and cruel Spirit. That actually felt like a better origin-story for something like a Cult of Fenris. And you wouldn\u2019t have a whole Tribe fall as one but instead split into two factions. Meanwhile, the Cult of Fenris isn\u2019t just members of that one fallen Tribe but as the name implies an actual cult that any Garou who has the same ideals and beliefs can join.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So in short Hauglosk is actually the result of a spiritual imbalance and not something inherent to the garou (also freaking called it!) and that CoF is not just a fallen tribe but a whole philosophy that stemmed from said imbalance meaning that even if main cult falls other similar sects will pop up as long as long said imbalance persists, which makes them a more subtle threat than how they're presented in the core book. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T21:18:04-07:00","id":1539514,"title":"","content":"So is the Wolf Matron/Patron split the canon explanation for W5 or like all the massive world building aspects in TBOHN just waffle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T23:35:50-07:00","id":1539516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review?p=1539514#post1539514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is the Wolf Matron/Patron split the canon explanation for W5 or like all the massive world building aspects in TBOHN just waffle?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like a reheated Rat God/Mother Rat duality, from the Ratkin and Revised Bone Gnawer books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T23:39:58-07:00","id":1539517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review?p=1539516#post1539516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's like a reheated Rat God/Mother Rat duality, from the Ratkin and Revised Bone Gnawer books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.....so CoF are Twitchers.....but still not Twitcher enough to be W5 RTs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T01:19:08-07:00","id":1539521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review?p=1539511#post1539511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in short Hauglosk is actually the result of a spiritual imbalance and not something inherent to the garou (also freaking called it!) and that CoF is not just a fallen tribe but a whole philosophy that stemmed from said imbalance meaning that even if main cult falls other similar sects will pop up as long as long said imbalance persists, which makes them a more subtle threat than how they're presented in the core book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's hard to say because the Cult of Fenris is still in the setting as this fallen Tribe (they talk about Maia's grandfather belonging to the Cult of Fenris... which in Heart of the Forest still had been called the Get of Fenris) but then you have this book which presents it as an ideology you can just adopt and not something limited to one fallen Tribe. And the split between Wolf-father and Wolf-mother gets described but it's never put into the context of the Cult of Fenris having Wolf as a Tribe-Patron-Spirit according to the W5 corebook. And then of course, there's the thing with Hauglosk where only the Wolf-mother-Spirit was able to diagnose Andrej with suffering from Hauglosk.<br /> <br /> In the end, it's all just about the writers of this game having their own somewhat different take on the W5 setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review?p=1539514#post1539514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is the Wolf Matron/Patron split the canon explanation for W5 or like all the massive world building aspects in TBOHN just waffle?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Different Tales' own take on it, more or less. Just like TBOHN.<br /> <br /> And canon... who even knows what that is anymore in W5. I bet the upcoming Shattered Nation supplement will only make this more confusing as the Renegade writers try to establish their own take on the W5 setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T04:11:38-07:00","id":1539524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review?p=1539521#post1539521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's hard to say because the Cult of Fenris is still in the setting as this fallen Tribe (they talk about Maia's grandfather belonging to the Cult of Fenris... which in Heart of the Forest still had been called the Get of Fenris) <b>but then you have this book which presents it as an ideology you can just adopt and not something limited to one fallen Tribe.</b><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think It would be wise for who ever in charge of writing future W5 material to actually lean into cult of as an ideology and decouple it from being exclusive to one tribe. It would go a long way to making them a credible threat and well maybe get rid of all that baggage with the get. Hell the could maybe even make the Get playable again (just say the younger members all collectively woke up pull a coup and have the newly reformed tribe be one of the most ardent hunters of the cult),<br /> <br /> Of course in all likely hood they just have the Cult do a White Howler and have them all simultaneously charge into spiral labyrinth and come out as BSD MK2 rather than actually make them playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T10:23:40-07:00","id":1539536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539465-w5-videogame-visual-novel-wta-purgatory-review?p=1539517#post1539517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep.....so CoF are Twitchers.....but still not Twitcher enough to be W5 RTs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, only the Twitchers are Twitchers*. The Bone Gnawers also fall under the same divison of Mother Rat/The Rat God, but don't gain explosive fury and magic arson powers out of it. They just stock up on weapons and get violent instead of looking out for the downtrodden as their primary MO.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*It feels really weird to say that given Amazon's livestreaming arm.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}